{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>With barbed hooks</b> — like \"[can you] put hooks in his eyes.\" The meaning: will his skin be filled with barbs so that you can take him?" "<b>Fish-spear</b> — it has no parallel. The meaning: like the likeness of a hook in the fish's jaw, by which fish are caught, which pierces the head."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:05:33.671377456Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}